<title>GERMANY: Opel names new supervisory board chief.</title>
<headline>Opel names new supervisory board chief.</headline>
<dateline>RUESSELSHEIM, Germany 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hans Wilhelm Gaeb is to replace Ferdinand Schwenger as head of Adam Opel AG's supervisory board when Schwenger retires June 30, Opel said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>Gaeb, who is vice president, public affairs for General Motors international operations in Zurich, has been a member of Opel's supervisory board since 1989.</p>
<p>The 60-year old Gaeb will also take over a new position as vice president of General Motors Europe and become a member of its strategy board.</p>
<p>Opel is a unit of General Motors Corp.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
